Attacking (angering) a peaceful creature gives you a -1 to your alignment
score (no matter what you are, lawful, neutral or chaotic), nothing to
really worry about.

There are selected peacefuls that give a greater hit to your alignment.
Your Quest leader is the most important one you do *not* want to kill,
co-aligned priests, quest guardians and pets coming next. Killing some
peaceful in one hit is also bad.

Killing a non-aligned priest (to Moloch, that is) or your Quest nemesis
gives you a big bonus.

Killing (or angering?) a non-peaceful should give you a bonus to your
alignment score, but I cannot find in the code by how much your score is
increased...

